<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!-- ============================================================================
         CTV v1 BASELINE, part 2 of 2: the CTV domain schema.

         THIS IS THE VERSION 1 BASELINE. Every DCRE database is dropped and recreated
         at the v1 cutover, so this changelog only ever runs against an EMPTY schema.
         That is why the usual re-run guards are absent, and their absence is
         deliberate rather than an oversight:

           - no ANY-checksum override. It existed because an external SQL file was
             edited after it had executed on live databases (A-81). With no recorded
             history there is no checksum to contradict, and suppressing checksum
             validation on a baseline would only disarm the control for every FUTURE
             edit.
           - the three layering columns are declared here rather than added by a
             later ALTER. version / created_at / updated_at arrived in
             2026/07/003-layering.xml as an additive retrofit onto a table that was
             already live. On an empty database the net result is one table with
             eight columns, so that is what this expresses. Carrying the create and
             the ALTER separately would reproduce the retrofit rather than the
             schema.
           - dcre_col.mandate is simply never created. 2026/08/001-drop-local-mandate
             dropped a mandates table that lived in the collections database and that
             no changelog created; in v1 it has no create to undo, so it has no drop
             either. A drop changeset in a baseline is scar tissue: it describes a
             database that no longer exists. CtvManifestParityTest asserts
             information_schema carries no relation named mandate, so the absence is
             tested rather than assumed. The DC-flow mandate gate reads
             dcre_man.man_ctv_view, the contract the mandates family owns.

         NO re-run guard is retained: see the changeset comment for the one that was
         and why it went. Pure typed tags throughout, no raw-SQL body.

         validation_log is CTV's table: CTV is its only writer (R-04), one row per
         validated detail record, keyed on the arrival and the record sequence.
         ============================================================================ -->

    <changeSet id="ctv-v1-validation-log" author="dcre">
        <!--
          NO re-run guard, like every other changeset in this baseline.

          An earlier draft of this file kept an onFail="MARK_RAN" tableExists guard,
          on the grounds that CRG minted validation_log as a bootstrap read-source
          and could win a pod-start race. CRG's own v1 rewrite removed that mint,
          along with its mint of every other relation it does not own, so the reason
          no longer holds. CTV is now the sole creator of validation_log in dcre_col,
          verified across the estate: the only other createTable tags for this name
          are payments ptv and payments prg, and both target dcre_pay, a different
          database.

          That makes the guard exactly what this baseline is meant to remove: one
          that cannot fire. Worse than dead, it carried a justification that had
          quietly become false, which is the more expensive kind of leftover,
          because the next reader would have believed it.
        -->
        <createTable tableName="validation_log">
            <column name="id" type="UUID" defaultValueComputed="gen_random_uuid()">
                <constraints primaryKey="true" nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="arrival_id" type="UUID">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="sequence" type="INT">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="outcome" type="VARCHAR(32)">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="detail" type="VARCHAR(256)"/>
            <column name="version" type="BIGINT" defaultValueNumeric="0">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="created_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="updated_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </createTable>
        <addUniqueConstraint tableName="validation_log" columnNames="arrival_id, sequence"
                             constraintName="uq_validation_arrival_sequence"/>
        <rollback>
            <dropTable tableName="validation_log"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
